              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "**wakehealth.edu** is the official website for **Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist** (formerly known as Wake Forest Baptist Health), a prominent, nationally recognized academic medical center and health system based in Winston-Salem, North Carolina.\n\nThe website serves as the primary digital portal for patients, students, researchers, and healthcare professionals. Below is an overview of the organization and what you can find on the website:\n\n### 1. Key Components of the Health System\n* **Clinical Enterprise:** The main hub is **Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist Medical Center** in Winston-Salem. The network also includes several regional community hospitals (such as Wilkes Medical Center, Lexington Medical Center, and Davie Medical Center), urgent care centers, and highly specialized clinics.\n* **Academic & Research Arm:** It is the home of the **Wake Forest University School of Medicine**, which serves as the academic core for the entire health system.\n* **Innovation Quarter:** An urban research park in downtown Winston-Salem that focuses on life sciences, biotechnology, and educational partnerships.\n\n### 2. Recent Mergers & Affiliations\n* **Combination with Atrium Health:** In 2021, Wake Forest Baptist Health officially integrated with Charlotte-based Atrium Health, rebranding the clinical enterprise to *Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist*. \n* **Integration into Advocate Health:** In late 2022, Atrium Health combined with Advocate Aurora Health to form **Advocate Health**, one of the largest non-profit health systems in the United States. Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist is a key academic anchor of this multi-state system.\n\n### 3. What You Can Do on the Website\n* **Patient Portal (MyAtriumHealth):** Patients can log into their secure Epic-based patient portal (formerly *MyWakeHealth*) to view lab results, message their doctors, request prescription refills, schedule appointments, and pay medical bills.\n* **Find a Doctor & Locations:** Users can search for primary care physicians, specialists, and specific clinical locations across Western North Carolina.\n* **Explore Medical Services:** The site provides information on specialized treatments, including their Level I Trauma Center, NCI-designated Comprehensive Cancer Center, and pediatric services.\n* **Education & Research:** For medical students, residents, and researchers, the site hosts directories for the Wake Forest School of Medicine, current clinical trials, and continuing medical education (CME).",
